# Compiled outputs of this client's Makefile.
#
# None of these was ignored before, which is how a macOS Mach-O
# `conformance_tracked` reached a commit: `git add demos/c-wire-client` swept up
# an untracked, unignored binary. A committed binary breaks CI in a way that
# looks nothing like its cause — the Linux runner checks the Mach-O out, make
# sees it newer than its sources and skips the rebuild, and the run dies with
# "Exec format error". `act` reproduced exactly that locally.
conformance
conformance_tracked
telemetry
negative
